WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.560
- Hello everyone.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:08.870
Welcome.

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:12.050
I'm Stephen Pitti, Professor
of History here at Yale

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.510
and Director of Yale Center
for the Study of Race,

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.980
Indigeneity and Transnational Migration.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.740
I'm delighted to see you all.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.850
On behalf of my colleagues

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:22.840
in the Yale Program for
the Study of Antisemitism,

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:24.750
especially my friend Maurice Samuels

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.600
who did so much to organize
this event, I wanna welcome you

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.620
to what should be a wonderful
discussion with Eric K. Ward,

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:36.100
that's entitled, Skin in
the Game: Antisemitism,

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.830
White Nationalism and the Work
for an Inclusive Democracy.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.320
Let me also thank Inessa
Laskova for her hard work

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.360
putting this event together.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.290
Thank you so much, Inessa.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.550
So, we have roughly an
hour here today, together.

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.810
Let me encourage everyone present

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.940
to consider putting your questions

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.237
that you have for Mr.
Ward into the Zoom Q&amp;A

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.790
and I'll do my best to read as
many of them as I can allow,

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:04.570
to Mr. Ward at the
conclusion of his remarks.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.940
So, please keep that in mind.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.030
Eric K. Ward, a nationally
recognized expert

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.630
on the relationship between
authoritarian movements,

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:18.010
hate violence and preserving
inclusive democracy,

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:23.010
is the recipient of the
2021 Civil Courage Prize,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.560
the first American to win that
award in its 21-year history.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.870
In his more than 30 years
civil rights career,

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.020
Eric's worked with community groups,

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:36.180
government and business
leaders, human rights advocates

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:41.120
and philanthropy as an organizer,
director, program officer,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.610
consultant and board member.

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.120
Eric's widely-quoted writings and speeches

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:50.490
are credited with key narrative
shifts in recent decades.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.890
He currently serves

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:55.040
as Executive Director
of Western State Center,

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.820
as Senior Fellow with the
Southern Poverty Law Center

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.250
and Race Forward and as
Co-chair for the Proteus Fund.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.890
Eric, thank you so much
for being with us today.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.540
We're really excited to have you.

00:02:06.808 --> 00:02:08.050
- Thanks.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:11.240
It is such a pleasure
to be with you today.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.303
I'm delighted to have this opportunity

00:02:14.303 --> 00:02:15.910
to speak with everyone,

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:18.630
of course, the question of antisemitism,

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.550
white nationalism and
the threat on democracy.

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:24.240
In the front of most Americans' minds,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.910
whether we are watching the beginning days

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:30.480
of a civil trial in Charlottesville

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.493
where

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.640
victims of neo-Nazis violence
from the Unite the Right riot

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.760
are seeking to hold
accountable the perpetrators,

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.270
whether we're looking at the
recent arrest and charges

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.833
of an individual who
set fire to a synagogue,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:57.100
or watching with great interest

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.330
how the federal government
will proceed in its prosecution

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.883
and investigation of the
January 6th insurrection,

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:07.780
the stress on democracy is very real.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:09.723
the rise of hate violence,

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.000
the increasing number of Americans

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.470
who believe that political violence

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.750
is the solution to our country's problems

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:24.920
and the answer to the
question of who is an American

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.130
and what will America
look like, are very real.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:32.830
This journey started for me back in

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.203
the late '80s.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.463
I had moved to Eugene, Oregon in 1986.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:45.160
I was part of the punk movement

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:48.460
in Southern California at the time,

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.740
was the lead singer of a
band, a garage punk band,

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:57.580
ska band, that went on to
be known as, "Sublime."

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:59.310
But as we were attending shows,

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.250
this kind of diverse creative set of folks

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:06.770
who found each other in a
new identity through music,

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.680
we began to notice some of the pressure

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.210
that was happening within the music scene,

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.560
within the hardcore punk scenes.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.210
Individuals were showing
up in increasing numbers,

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:20.400
who were calling themselves
white power punks

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:23.933
and eventually calling
themselves neo-Nazi skinheads.

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:29.470
They were very intent on both
policing and criminalizing

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:34.470
those who they felt didn't
belong within those communities.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:39.373
Eventually I moved up to
Eugene, Oregon in 1986.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:42.340
When I moved up, right before me,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.480
another individual had moved
up from Southern California.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.430
He was older than me.

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:47.330
He was retired.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.170
His name was Richard Butler.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:53.830
And Richard Butler was a
retired aircraft mechanic,

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.660
former World War II Vet

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.570
and recently retired from Hughes Aircraft.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.330
He relocated to the Northwest.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.720
Not Oregon, but to a place called Idaho,

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.720
a town called Hayden Lake
and he restarted his church,

00:05:10.378 --> 00:05:13.550
Church of Jesus Christ
Christian-Aryan Nations.

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.530
The Aryan Nations taught three things.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:20.010
The first was that Jews are
the literal children of Satan.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:23.160
The second was that People of Color

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:26.670
were referred to a subhuman, chattel,

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:30.140
meaning humans without souls.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.830
And the third was that

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.840
the Aryan Nations and
Richard Butler taught

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.700
that the United States was
to be a new Aryan homeland

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:41.320
and that the Pacific Northwest

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.750
would be the beginnings of that

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:47.960
white revolution.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:51.970
It is in that period that
I first came to understand

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:56.230
that racism wasn't merely
a set of behaviors,

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.640
that it was also a social
movement phenomenon.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.910
Eventually I came to understand
that what I was looking at

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.760
were the emergence of a movement

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.623
we now know to be white nationalism.

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:12.260
I was a young activist then

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.680
and I think it's important to say,

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.960
this was before the internet.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.400
And as we joined together with others

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.760
to try to manage this
violence in organizing,

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.200
we collected flyers.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.430
Those flyers for often warnings

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:29.480
of further violence, or harassment.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.590
This was a period of great upheaval

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:37.140
by the white nationalist movement
in the Pacific Northwest.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.930
They believed that the Pacific Northwest

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:41.720
was the beginnings of that homeland

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:44.100
and they engaged in acts of violence,

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:47.500
including the assassination
of a radio talk show host

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.650
by the name of Alan Berg
in Denver, Colorado,

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.140
the murder beating death
of an Ethiopian student

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.520
by the name of Mulugeta Seraw

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.190
who was attacked on his way
home one night from school

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:03.240
and beaten to death with a baseball bat

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:05.670
by neo-Nazi skinheads.

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:08.420
These were just a few of the incidences

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:10.950
that occurred here in
the Pacific Northwest.

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:14.330
In truth, much of what
the nation faces now,

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.700
was first experienced
nearly three decades ago

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.730
here in the Pacific Northwest.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:23.490
At the time it was hard to
get the nation's attention

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.750
and in fact, until Charlottesville,

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:29.460
it was very hard to get the
nation's attention focused

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:33.250
on the fact that racism
was not only systemic,

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:35.530
but a social movement phenomenon

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:38.720
and that those social
movements actually pivoted

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.330
our understanding of what
was acceptable in society.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.410
But these were the movements
we were monitoring.

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:47.200
And as we were collecting those flyers

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:51.340
I was telling you about, we
began to notice something.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:52.990
Those who had done this work before us,

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.320
began to point this out,
that all the fliers,

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:01.320
no matter how overtly racist,
anti-Black, or anti-Latino,

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:05.220
or no matter how
anti-Muslim, or homophobic,

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.850
or anti-immigrant,

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:11.090
there was always some
antisemitic caricature

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.980
of a Jewish figure, or
symbol on these flyers.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:18.300
It didn't matter whether
they were attacking

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:21.880
those who have been
diagnosed with HIV/Aids.

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.590
It didn't matter whether
they're going after immigrants,

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:29.590
or the media, or African
Americans, or Latinos, or women,

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:33.860
there was always this caricature.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:38.860
And it is when we began to
understand one simple truth,

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.180
which was, antisemitism
wasn't simply at the core

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.630
of this white nationalist movement.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.700
That it was the core of white nationalism

00:08:49.573 --> 00:08:53.330
and that it was so central
to white nationalism

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:58.010
that I, as a anti-racist,
racial justice activist,

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:02.200
seeking Black liberation,
quickly came to understand

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:04.640
that we and other marginalized groups

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:08.260
would never achieve opportunity and equity

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:11.020
if we were not also active in the struggle

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:14.483
to uproot this form of anti-Jewish hate.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:18.510
Amongst 21st century white nationalists,

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:21.450
Jews were being cast in the same role

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.080
that they had always
filled for antisemites,

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.930
as the absolute others,

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:28.720
demons stirring a pot of lesser evils

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.283
and the driving force
behind white dispossession.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.200
As I wrote in, "Skin in the Game,"

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:40.060
outlining the white nationalist worldview,

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:44.670
at the foundation of that
movement was an explicit claim

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:47.110
that Jews were a separate race.

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.810
This is really critical for us to hold.

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:53.290
What I'm trying to
unearth here and lift up,

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:56.440
is that for the white
nationalist movement,

00:09:56.440 --> 00:10:00.530
their hatred of Jews was not
a religious form of bigotry.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:05.530
Jews weren't cast as a religion,
but as a separate race.

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:11.560
And it filled the same role
that has always been filled

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:16.143
by antisemites, placing
Jews has the absolute other,

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.040
demons stirring a pot of lesser evils,

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:23.403
the driving force behind
white dispossession.

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:29.560
It was an explicit claim that
Jews were a separate race,

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.500
that they weren't white

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:34.630
and that their ostensible
position as white

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:37.066
was merely a trick,

00:10:37.066 --> 00:10:39.440
the greatest trick that
the devil ever played

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:41.460
in the words of the time

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:42.900
of a leading white nationalist figure

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.700
by the name of Pete Peters,

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.100
who was a counterpart of Richard Butler

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.663
and his Aryan Nations.

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:52.580
For Pete Peters and the
white nationalist group,

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:55.880
Jews, despite and indeed
because of the fact

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:59.890
that they were seen as white,
were placed as an enemy race

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:03.090
that must be exposed and eliminated.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:07.310
It is often why I tell people
that antisemitism is core

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.070
to white nationalist ideology.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:10.360
It is central.

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:12.730
It is their worldview.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:17.570
It is that fantasy of
invisible Jewish power

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:21.540
that explains for white
nationalists how Black Americans,

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.433
a race of supposed inferiors,

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.960
could orchestrate the end of Jim Crow,

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:30.210
or how feminists and the LGBTQ community

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:33.110
could upend traditional gender roles,

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.970
or even how immigrant
workers in this country

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:39.470
could mount a challenge,
successful challenge,

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.870
to economic inequality.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:45.350
Folks often asked me
over these last 30 years.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:47.220
It was 30 years ago that I attended

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:51.440
my first white nationalist
meeting to monitor that meeting.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.110
The reason I attended
was that, at the time,

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.500
again, we couldn't Google things.

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.350
We had to go sit in meetings.

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:05.050
We had to read their writings
and listened to their talks.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.930
And I simply wasn't going to
ask people to do something

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.730
I hadn't done myself.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:12.900
So, I walked into many of these meetings.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:16.180
Now, these weren't the
hardcore neo-Nazi meetings.

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:17.820
These were the coalitional meetings

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:20.560
that looked much like the alt-right today.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:24.730
White nationalist, tax resisters,

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:27.250
paramilitary figures and others

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:30.330
who were building the first vestiges

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:33.280
of what we now know to be the alt-right.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:35.450
How was I accepted in these meetings?

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.990
Well, the truth is, I was accepted

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:42.990
because these groupings saw
Jews as their primary enemy.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.120
Not Black people, not
other People of Color.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.920
Certainly we were challenging
and we were trouble,

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.630
but we were placed as the puppets

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:57.280
of our Jewish puppet masters.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.620
They were willing to place me

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:02.240
in the role of a potential ally.

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.740
In the words of one leading

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:08.060
white nationalist figure
at the time, Louis Beam,

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.230
he called for a new multi-racialism

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.590
within the white nationalist movement.

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.170
At least a multi-racial coalition.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.130
In the words of one of his counterparts,

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:21.290
in a meeting in Estes Park, Colorado

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:25.200
leading up to Oklahoma City,

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.300
one of his counterparts announced,

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:30.170
first we deal with the federal government,

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:33.330
then we deal with the
question of the Jews.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:37.040
That is why a multi-racial coalition

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:39.150
against the government is called for,

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.883
in the words of white nationalism.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:45.837
Folks often ask me,
"Where is the antisemitism

00:13:45.837 --> 00:13:47.850
"in the white nationalism?"

00:13:47.850 --> 00:13:50.220
My response is, "It's everywhere."

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.580
When the Tree of Life shooter

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:57.030
said Jews were committing a
genocide against white people,

00:13:57.030 --> 00:14:00.530
he was using language that
was intimately familiar

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:03.000
to his fellow white nationalists.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:07.470
It is such rabid antisemitism
that is the framework

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:11.250
in which this entire movement functions.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.740
But let's be clear about something.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.320
White nationalists
don't bring antisemitism

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:17.940
to our community.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:22.890
They merely organize the
bigotry that already exists.

00:14:22.890 --> 00:14:27.070
Is often why I say as
an anti-racist activist,

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:31.470
one of the things that is
fundamental to my beliefs,

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:35.700
is that to refuse to deal with
any ideology of domination

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.460
is to abet it.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:41.430
Fighting antisemitism cuts
off the animating force

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:43.000
of white nationalism

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.823
for the sake of all
marginalized communities.

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.033
In this moment,

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:50.430
we in this country

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:53.253
are dealing with two
significant phenomena.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.010
The persistent and historic nature

00:14:57.010 --> 00:14:59.800
and impact of white supremacy,

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:02.800
a system grounded on white superiority,

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:06.020
a belief that skin color

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:11.020
dictates one's place and value in society.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:15.250
It is made up on an
eye on the false notion

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:19.780
that race is a real biological
definition, which it is not.

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.297
What we understand is that white supremacy

00:15:22.297 --> 00:15:25.620
and the concept of race
is a social construct

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:30.460
largely created in order
to establish social control

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:32.130
in our society.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:36.530
It is what allowed the
quick and fast development

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:41.530
of the United States into a
global economic powerhouse.

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:46.610
White supremacy was grounded
upon three specific principles.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.350
The first was the stolen
resources and land

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:51.870
of Native people.

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:56.040
The second was a system of chattel slavery

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:59.580
that was like none other

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:02.870
that stripped Black people of
their language, their culture,

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.070
their religions, their very relationships

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:10.010
and reconstructed them
into Black Americans.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:15.010
It was those hundreds of years
of free labor in this country

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:16.880
that positioned the United States

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:19.650
as the economic power it is today.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:22.250
But beyond the stolen resources

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:25.770
and genocide of Native people,
beyond chattel slavery,

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:27.460
there was a third pillar

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:29.830
in the construction of white supremacy

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:34.830
and that was the control of
women and sexuality in society.

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:40.690
These were three critical
pillars of white supremacy.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:43.720
Then along comes this
1960 civil rights movement

00:16:44.846 --> 00:16:47.160
and this 1960 civil rights movement

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:50.520
overthrows white supremacy
as the rule of law.

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:52.740
Now, I wanna be clear about something.

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:56.430
I'm not saying that white
supremacy no longer exists

00:16:56.430 --> 00:16:57.850
in America.

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.720
I can attest, as an African American male,

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.350
that it exists very much in our society.

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.660
What I'm saying, is that previous

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.200
to the victories of the
civil rights movement,

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:12.770
white supremacy was the uncontested lens

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:17.340
upon which most of us understood society

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:21.393
whether we were talking about
culture, politics, economics.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:26.263
Then the civil rights movement wins.

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:29.370
It creates other lenses.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:34.370
Pluralism, racial justice,
lenses of equity, right?

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:39.970
And it is in that moment that
those who were conditioned

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:43.960
to see themselves as superior
because of their skin tone,

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:47.300
were thrown into an existential crisis.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:49.620
How could they explain that they lost

00:17:49.620 --> 00:17:52.260
to those they saw as inferior?

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.300
That was impossible.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.670
To acknowledge that they
lost that moral fight

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:01.110
would be to acknowledge
the agency and humanity

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:01.983
of Black people.

00:18:02.928 --> 00:18:05.350
And that simply wasn't going to happen.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.610
Not because people were bad,

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:10.530
but because they had been
conditioned in every way

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.443
to see Black people as inferior.

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:17.440
So, they constructed
an answer to this loss.

00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.040
The construction borrowed from,

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.037
the, "Protocols of the
Learned Elders of Zion,"

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:27.210
a fictional antisemitic
account from Europe

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:32.180
in the early 1900s that was
spread by Russian secret police

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:36.740
who were afraid of the spread
of democracy in Europe,

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:40.540
particularly in places
like Germany and France.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:45.250
This false narrative, steeped
in antisemitic tropes,

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.360
purported to tell a story of Jewish elders

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:51.340
who gathered at midnight in a cemetery

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:53.940
to plot the takeover of the world,

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.130
to the control of the economy,

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:59.323
culture, finance, et cetera.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:02.710
Now, we should be clear,

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.700
this narrative was a strong narrative

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:11.320
because it understood that fear
and xenophobia towards Jews

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:14.360
already existed in society.

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:15.850
As I said,

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:18.240
white nationalists
don't bring antisemitism

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:19.870
to our communities.

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:24.810
They merely organize the
antisemitism that already exist.

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:28.990
Good organizers don't
try to inject new ideas

00:19:28.990 --> 00:19:30.793
in order to galvanize communities.

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:35.000
They merely try to tap into the ideas

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:38.090
that already exist in a community.

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:41.660
So too was it in the early
days of the Protocols.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.290
But it also was a strong narrative.

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:45.750
How strong of a narrative

00:19:47.013 --> 00:19:49.450
were the, "Protocols of
Learned Elders of Zion?"

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:52.690
Well, we are bombarded with
that narrative constantly

00:19:52.690 --> 00:19:54.730
in unconscious ways.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:58.520
Not because people understand
the original narrative,

00:19:58.520 --> 00:20:00.620
but because that is how influential,

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.603
I believe, it has been in the society.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:05.360
I'll give you an example.

00:20:05.360 --> 00:20:07.230
You don't have to read The Protocols

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:09.700
to actually understand The Protocols.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:13.540
I often ask people if they've
ever heard of a TV show

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:17.910
from the 1990s, or early
2000s, called the X-Files,

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:20.830
produced and directed by Chris Carter.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:24.080
It is a story of two FBI agents

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:27.710
who stumble upon a global conspiracy,

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:32.360
a conspiracy to infect the body politic

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:34.733
through the injection of an alien virus.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.250
The aliens have made an appearance.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.490
They're hiding amongst humans

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.370
and are slowly corrupting our leaders

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:46.350
and taking control of culture and finance

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:49.300
in order to prepare for this invasion.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:53.180
And it's merely two FBI agents
who have discovered the truth

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:56.680
and no one believes them
and their job is to wake up

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:59.313
the rest of the world to this conspiracy.

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:02.840
If you've ever seen the X-Files,

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:05.680
or many alien invasion stories,

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:10.680
you too actually already
understand the ground narrative

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:14.080
of the, "Protocols of the
Learned Elders of Zion."

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:16.450
Now, I have to give a disclaimer here.

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:19.360
I'm not here to say Chris
Carter is antisemitic,

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.410
or even that the X-Files are antisemitic.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:25.330
What I'm trying to help people understand

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:28.920
is that antisemitism
functions on a spectrum

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:32.370
from the conscious to
the unconscious level.

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:37.370
If antisemitism continues to
spread in the United States,

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:41.660
if the white nationalist movement
taps into it effectively,

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:45.220
it is because it is already existent.

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:49.370
It's often why I say,
there is no left, or right,

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.940
or conservative, or liberal.

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:53.610
Antisemitism.

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:56.740
There's merely antisemitism in society

00:21:56.740 --> 00:22:00.040
and how we tap into it to build power.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.300
And this is my next point.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:04.160
We should understand

00:22:04.160 --> 00:22:07.220
the white nationalist movement
isn't spreading antisemitism,

00:22:07.220 --> 00:22:11.730
or even other forms of bigotry
in order to spread bigotry.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.940
They're merely organizing the bigotry

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:19.600
to build political power,
to reshape the society.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:20.770
Into what?

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.630
Well, let me explain.

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:25.440
I talked about white supremacy earlier,

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:29.120
a historic and present-day
system of inequality,

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:34.120
discrimination and exploitation,
one that still exists

00:22:34.160 --> 00:22:36.220
in the defacto state

00:22:36.220 --> 00:22:40.130
and was once the sole rule
of law in this country,

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:42.811
successfully turned back by
the civil rights movement

00:22:42.811 --> 00:22:45.230
of the 1960s, as I explained.

00:22:45.230 --> 00:22:47.980
I talked about how those
who believed in Jim Crow

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.373
and separate but equal,

00:22:50.270 --> 00:22:53.160
could not accept that
they lost to Black people

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:54.270
because they've been conditioned

00:22:54.270 --> 00:22:55.863
to see themselves as inferior,

00:22:57.270 --> 00:22:59.540
uh, superior to Black people.

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:03.690
But the Protocols became
a very convenient answer.

00:23:03.690 --> 00:23:06.520
For them they could state

00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:09.320
that they didn't lose to Black
people because as we said,

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:11.020
in their eyes that was impossible.

00:23:12.060 --> 00:23:17.060
Instead they lost to this
global Jewish conspiracy.

00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:21.110
If white supremacy, the
system of exploitation,

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:23.730
was built upon the paper of anti-Blackness

00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:26.070
and the genocide of Native people,

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:29.160
white nationalism was
written upon the paper

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:31.160
of antisemitism.

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:33.160
It's often why I say to people

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:36.800
that we must not conflate the two terms.

00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:40.040
When we conflate a system
with a social movement,

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:43.340
it confuses us in the
tools that are needed

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:47.610
to respond to effectively
to each phenomenon.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:50.610
I often liken, comparing,
or conflating the two

00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:54.720
to comparing a cow in a Big Mac.

00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:59.000
Now look, both a cow and a
Big Mac are made out of beef,

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.920
but when one drops their
Big Mac on the ground,

00:24:01.920 --> 00:24:04.500
you don't call a veterinarian.

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:08.233
When we conflate systems
with social movements,

00:24:10.002 --> 00:24:13.563
we confuse the necessary
tools needed to address both.

00:24:14.540 --> 00:24:16.730
But there's also another danger

00:24:16.730 --> 00:24:19.960
that we get into debates around hire.

00:24:19.960 --> 00:24:22.570
Which one has more effect?

00:24:22.570 --> 00:24:25.890
Well, the truth is that both
are undercutting democracy

00:24:25.890 --> 00:24:27.720
in the society.

00:24:27.720 --> 00:24:30.030
The civil rights move of the 1960s

00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:33.883
through its defeat of white
supremacy under the rule of law,

00:24:34.830 --> 00:24:39.560
brought democracy into full
life in the United States.

00:24:39.560 --> 00:24:41.200
Now, not complete life,

00:24:41.200 --> 00:24:44.060
so please don't be a literalist with me.

00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:46.570
Let's understand both social movements

00:24:46.570 --> 00:24:50.550
and conditions in society unfold and flow

00:24:50.550 --> 00:24:53.270
along arcs on time.

00:24:53.270 --> 00:24:56.510
What I mean, is that we understand,

00:24:56.510 --> 00:24:58.710
in the words of John Lewis,

00:24:58.710 --> 00:25:02.770
that before the 1960
civil rights movement,

00:25:02.770 --> 00:25:05.443
democracy was merely an aspiration.

00:25:06.370 --> 00:25:08.780
The advent and success

00:25:08.780 --> 00:25:11.030
of the civil rights movement of the 1960s

00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:17.130
evolved democracy from
an aspiration to reality.

00:25:17.130 --> 00:25:20.170
The role of our generation is to secure

00:25:20.170 --> 00:25:23.120
and continue to advance that reality.

00:25:23.120 --> 00:25:26.970
But there is now a backlash, for you see,

00:25:26.970 --> 00:25:29.860
the white nationalist
movement isn't best thought of

00:25:29.860 --> 00:25:32.370
as a revolutionary movement.

00:25:32.370 --> 00:25:36.610
It actually is best
thought of as a backlash.

00:25:36.610 --> 00:25:38.540
A backlash against the victories

00:25:38.540 --> 00:25:41.130
of the 1960s civil rights movement,

00:25:41.130 --> 00:25:43.560
a movement that has slowly been growing

00:25:44.872 --> 00:25:48.290
for the last four decades in this country,

00:25:48.290 --> 00:25:51.500
a movement that has been
growing without much response.

00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:55.250
You see, social movements
don't appear out of thin air.

00:25:55.250 --> 00:25:57.650
You know that 1960s civil rights movement

00:25:57.650 --> 00:25:59.140
I keep referencing?

00:25:59.140 --> 00:26:01.190
Well, if you talk to actual historians

00:26:01.190 --> 00:26:03.230
who may be listening on this call,

00:26:03.230 --> 00:26:05.290
they will tell you without a doubt,

00:26:05.290 --> 00:26:09.757
the 1960s civil rights movement
didn't start in the 1960s.

00:26:09.757 --> 00:26:11.720
In fact, most of the major victories

00:26:11.720 --> 00:26:16.650
of the civil right movement
occurred in the mid 1950s.

00:26:16.650 --> 00:26:21.370
Rosa Parks, Little Rock,
Brown vs. Board of Education,

00:26:21.370 --> 00:26:22.453
to name a few.

00:26:23.330 --> 00:26:26.470
But even as you talk to these
academics who're well-versed

00:26:26.470 --> 00:26:28.440
on the history of the
civil rights movement,

00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:30.640
they will tell you something else.

00:26:30.640 --> 00:26:32.880
That that 1960s civil rights movement

00:26:32.880 --> 00:26:35.640
didn't get underway in the 1950s,

00:26:35.640 --> 00:26:38.380
but in the 1930s and '40s.

00:26:38.380 --> 00:26:42.270
Social movements grow
and influence over time.

00:26:42.270 --> 00:26:45.330
And the mistake we have
made as racial justice

00:26:45.330 --> 00:26:48.020
and human rights
activists in this country,

00:26:48.020 --> 00:26:49.680
is that we have assumed

00:26:49.680 --> 00:26:52.220
that we are the only social movements

00:26:52.220 --> 00:26:54.630
on the game board of democracy.

00:26:54.630 --> 00:26:58.840
That we are the only social
movements that matter.

00:26:58.840 --> 00:27:01.870
Our own arrogance has left our communities

00:27:01.870 --> 00:27:04.320
and in the 75 years of sacrifice

00:27:04.320 --> 00:27:07.643
of those who came before us,
vulnerable in this moment.

00:27:08.670 --> 00:27:10.220
You see, the white nationalist movement

00:27:10.220 --> 00:27:12.400
understands one thing,

00:27:12.400 --> 00:27:16.340
that a pluralist democracy
is its worst nightmare.

00:27:16.340 --> 00:27:19.313
That a successful
democracy that functions,

00:27:20.550 --> 00:27:23.030
that is people-centered, accountable

00:27:24.615 --> 00:27:29.615
and transparent, undermines
the white nationalists' fear

00:27:30.020 --> 00:27:32.713
and existential crisis, right?

00:27:33.720 --> 00:27:37.300
What we have to understand moving forward,

00:27:37.300 --> 00:27:42.150
is that we need to reevaluate
the importance of democracy.

00:27:42.150 --> 00:27:44.140
I understand the cynicism.

00:27:44.140 --> 00:27:45.770
I'm a Black man in America

00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:49.280
and I understand the rage of mistreatment

00:27:49.280 --> 00:27:54.130
and the incompleteness of
democracy and how it has been used

00:27:54.130 --> 00:27:55.920
to protect inequality,

00:27:55.920 --> 00:27:58.733
both here in the United States and abroad.

00:27:59.690 --> 00:28:04.150
But we also have to
understand that the democracy,

00:28:04.150 --> 00:28:05.690
that those who came before us,

00:28:05.690 --> 00:28:09.370
sacrificed, died and struggled to bill,

00:28:09.370 --> 00:28:12.530
has brought more to this country,

00:28:12.530 --> 00:28:16.000
to marginalized communities
and white folks,

00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:18.563
than any other ideology to date.

00:28:19.410 --> 00:28:23.440
We should understand that
democracy, inclusive democracy,

00:28:23.440 --> 00:28:28.440
participatory democracy, that
makes real this Republic,

00:28:28.560 --> 00:28:33.063
is one of the most radical
ideologies ever in existence.

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:36.980
White nationalists don't
like it because the truth is,

00:28:36.980 --> 00:28:38.970
is that the democracy

00:28:38.970 --> 00:28:42.053
that these civil rights activists built,

00:28:42.990 --> 00:28:47.240
has delivered more for white
America than white supremacy

00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:51.373
and the white nationalist
movement ever can and ever will.

00:28:52.220 --> 00:28:56.650
Democracy, for the white
nationalist movement is a threat

00:28:56.650 --> 00:28:59.170
because it makes a lie of their argument

00:29:00.050 --> 00:29:03.203
that race war is
inevitable in this country.

00:29:04.300 --> 00:29:05.763
But we should understand,

00:29:06.860 --> 00:29:10.520
if we want to know the real
threat towards democracy,

00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:13.180
it isn't the white nationalist movement.

00:29:13.180 --> 00:29:16.160
We have to be brave enough
to pick up the mirror

00:29:16.160 --> 00:29:17.433
and to take a look in it.

00:29:18.400 --> 00:29:22.610
I reflect on a rally that took place

00:29:22.610 --> 00:29:25.060
four, or five years ago now.

00:29:25.060 --> 00:29:26.430
Took place here in Portland, Oregon.

00:29:26.430 --> 00:29:28.680
It was an alt-right protest.

00:29:28.680 --> 00:29:33.220
So, counter-protesters
showed up and so did others.

00:29:33.220 --> 00:29:36.247
At one point, as I was
monitoring this rally,

00:29:36.247 --> 00:29:37.730
(Eric coughs)
I'm trying to understand

00:29:37.730 --> 00:29:40.950
what the level of
mobilization was in the city.

00:29:40.950 --> 00:29:44.089
I noticed an alt-right
activist sitting down.

00:29:44.089 --> 00:29:45.190
And there was a guy with a camera

00:29:45.190 --> 00:29:48.390
who had it shoved in his
face and screaming at him

00:29:48.390 --> 00:29:49.570
and demanding that this

00:29:49.570 --> 00:29:52.540
alt-right white nationalist
activist explain

00:29:52.540 --> 00:29:54.003
why he was here in Portland.

00:29:54.910 --> 00:29:58.070
Didn't he know the city of
Portland didn't want him?

00:29:58.070 --> 00:30:01.290
Didn't he know counter-protesters
didn't want him?

00:30:01.290 --> 00:30:04.590
Didn't he know the mayor
of Portland didn't want him

00:30:04.590 --> 00:30:06.360
here in the city?

00:30:06.360 --> 00:30:11.230
And why was he here, the
camera man demanded an answer.

00:30:11.230 --> 00:30:14.470
What this white nationalist activist said

00:30:14.470 --> 00:30:16.863
is worthy of us paying attention to.

00:30:18.200 --> 00:30:19.617
He looked at the guy and he said,

00:30:19.617 --> 00:30:21.927
"I've heard we're not wanted here.

00:30:21.927 --> 00:30:25.387
"But the truth is, is
that Portland," he said,

00:30:25.387 --> 00:30:28.637
"is a shrinking Black population

00:30:28.637 --> 00:30:31.700
"by both percentage and whole number."

00:30:31.700 --> 00:30:32.573
It's a true fact.

00:30:33.530 --> 00:30:37.177
He then went on to say, "You
can say you don't want us here,

00:30:37.177 --> 00:30:41.127
"but you're doing something
we could never get away with.

00:30:41.127 --> 00:30:43.417
"You are actually disappearing

00:30:43.417 --> 00:30:45.930
"the Black people of Portland, Oregon."

00:30:45.930 --> 00:30:48.030
That was his response.

00:30:48.030 --> 00:30:51.450
In short, he was calling us hypocrites.

00:30:51.450 --> 00:30:56.130
You see, each day that we
allow systemic inequality

00:30:56.130 --> 00:31:00.630
to exist in our society,
we further mark ourselves

00:31:00.630 --> 00:31:04.970
as the hypocrites of a
pluralistic, multicultural,

00:31:04.970 --> 00:31:07.313
multiracial democracy.

00:31:08.280 --> 00:31:10.050
When we leave unchecked

00:31:10.050 --> 00:31:14.720
the issues of segregation
in housing, in employment,

00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:17.573
in education, in health,

00:31:18.640 --> 00:31:22.250
we do the work of white nationalism.

00:31:22.250 --> 00:31:25.550
We help lift it up as the alternative.

00:31:25.550 --> 00:31:28.930
We are in a moment of great
populism in this country.

00:31:28.930 --> 00:31:32.930
Very few people are
interested in the status quo.

00:31:32.930 --> 00:31:34.070
Why?

00:31:34.070 --> 00:31:38.660
The status quo has not benefited
the majority of Americans,

00:31:38.660 --> 00:31:41.023
whether they are People
of Color, or white.

00:31:41.960 --> 00:31:45.110
People want and demand

00:31:45.110 --> 00:31:48.163
new ways of walking through society.

00:31:49.360 --> 00:31:52.430
The answer that the
status quo is sufficient,

00:31:52.430 --> 00:31:55.440
is not a sufficient answer.

00:31:55.440 --> 00:31:58.340
Instead, we have to make real

00:31:58.340 --> 00:32:01.960
the promise of a multiracial democracy.

00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:05.993
One that people can practice
and taste each and every day.

00:32:06.830 --> 00:32:10.380
If we don't do this, let's be clear,

00:32:10.380 --> 00:32:13.380
people will increasingly choose the vision

00:32:13.380 --> 00:32:15.030
of white nationalism.

00:32:15.030 --> 00:32:15.863
Why?

00:32:15.863 --> 00:32:18.630
It's one that everyone understands.

00:32:18.630 --> 00:32:22.670
When I say the words,
"Make America Great Again,"

00:32:22.670 --> 00:32:25.330
you don't have to ask
me what that looks like,

00:32:25.330 --> 00:32:28.660
what that sounds like,
what that feels like.

00:32:28.660 --> 00:32:30.880
We see it each and every day

00:32:30.880 --> 00:32:34.270
and we knew it even before
the words were uttered.

00:32:34.270 --> 00:32:36.800
But when we say inclusive democracy,

00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:39.690
when we say a pluralist society,

00:32:39.690 --> 00:32:43.440
we have not set visions
of what that looks like.

00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:46.260
We have to understand,

00:32:46.260 --> 00:32:49.310
people will pick the future that they know

00:32:49.310 --> 00:32:53.450
even if it is unhealthy
for them, over the unknown,

00:32:53.450 --> 00:32:55.820
nearly every time.

00:32:55.820 --> 00:32:58.760
It's important that we
continue to move forward

00:32:58.760 --> 00:33:01.510
to make our society responsive

00:33:01.510 --> 00:33:03.813
and to bring opportunity to all Americans.

00:33:04.730 --> 00:33:06.030
But the white nationalist movement

00:33:06.030 --> 00:33:08.460
understands something else too.

00:33:08.460 --> 00:33:11.690
That antisemitism isn't just an attack

00:33:11.690 --> 00:33:13.590
on the Jewish community.

00:33:13.590 --> 00:33:16.910
It is a way of undermining
belief in democracy

00:33:18.100 --> 00:33:20.810
by providing a conspiratorial worldview

00:33:20.810 --> 00:33:23.570
that provides very simple answers

00:33:23.570 --> 00:33:28.290
and allows us to put our
fears onto a small community,

00:33:28.290 --> 00:33:29.483
the Jewish community.

00:33:30.720 --> 00:33:33.210
But it's not just in that way.

00:33:33.210 --> 00:33:35.250
We should understand as People of Color,

00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:37.150
immigrants and women,

00:33:37.150 --> 00:33:40.980
that antisemitism is a much
of a physical threat to us

00:33:40.980 --> 00:33:43.450
as it is the Jewish community.

00:33:43.450 --> 00:33:45.820
Whether we are talking about attacks,

00:33:45.820 --> 00:33:48.010
the mass shootings in El Paso,

00:33:48.010 --> 00:33:50.800
targeting Latinos at a Walmart,

00:33:50.800 --> 00:33:54.310
or the targeting of Sikhs in Wisconsin,

00:33:54.310 --> 00:33:57.140
or the targeting of African
American church-goers

00:33:57.140 --> 00:34:00.090
in Charlotte, South Carolina,

00:34:00.090 --> 00:34:03.483
or the targeting of Jews in Pittsburgh,

00:34:04.370 --> 00:34:09.280
in each case the killer
believed that they were engaging

00:34:09.280 --> 00:34:12.293
in an existential war
with the Jewish community.

00:34:13.220 --> 00:34:16.440
That's because antisemitism,
as I said before,

00:34:16.440 --> 00:34:19.410
is not merely a set of behaviors,

00:34:19.410 --> 00:34:21.993
but an ideology and a worldview.

00:34:23.270 --> 00:34:26.310
I think I am not exaggerating

00:34:26.310 --> 00:34:29.450
to argue that most
mission-oriented hate crimes

00:34:29.450 --> 00:34:34.110
in the United States were
largely driven by antisemitism

00:34:34.110 --> 00:34:38.390
regardless of who the actual victims were.

00:34:38.390 --> 00:34:41.670
So, those of us who are
non-Jewish have to understand

00:34:41.670 --> 00:34:44.730
that we are as much at
risk to antisemitism

00:34:44.730 --> 00:34:49.060
as the Jewish community
is and the democracy

00:34:49.060 --> 00:34:50.743
that we have struggled to build.

00:34:51.620 --> 00:34:53.313
So, how do we move forward?

00:34:54.220 --> 00:34:59.220
First of all, we need large,
vibrant, national debates

00:34:59.690 --> 00:35:00.973
on antisemitism.

00:35:01.980 --> 00:35:06.220
It means leaning in to
courageous conversation.

00:35:06.220 --> 00:35:09.820
Until we as a society
start naming antisemitism

00:35:09.820 --> 00:35:11.890
and the antisemitic tropes,

00:35:11.890 --> 00:35:15.980
we will continue to play
them out as unconscious bias,

00:35:15.980 --> 00:35:19.980
both individually and as a society.

00:35:19.980 --> 00:35:23.870
Because antisemitism denies the agency

00:35:23.870 --> 00:35:27.530
of marginalized communities
with legitimate grievances,

00:35:27.530 --> 00:35:31.140
antisemitism becomes a convenient excuse

00:35:31.140 --> 00:35:34.980
by those who seek to
backlash and to clamp down

00:35:34.980 --> 00:35:37.433
on the push for racial
justice in this country.

00:35:38.270 --> 00:35:42.900
And finally, antisemitism
provides simple answers

00:35:42.900 --> 00:35:45.300
to the complex and nuanced conversations

00:35:45.300 --> 00:35:47.500
we need to be having.

00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:50.810
Understanding antisemitism
helps protect you

00:35:50.810 --> 00:35:54.390
from the dog whistle
politics that are in play.

00:35:54.390 --> 00:35:58.690
When we hear terms like globalist,
or Eastern establishment,

00:35:58.690 --> 00:36:02.080
or even the media being bandied about,

00:36:02.080 --> 00:36:06.010
those who are well-versed in
the tropes of antisemitism

00:36:06.010 --> 00:36:10.450
understand many of the
conversations that are happening

00:36:10.450 --> 00:36:12.210
at a conscious level.

00:36:12.210 --> 00:36:15.840
But let's be clear, at
the unconscious level

00:36:15.840 --> 00:36:18.180
all of us are being impacted

00:36:18.180 --> 00:36:20.940
by these antisemitic narratives.

00:36:20.940 --> 00:36:23.410
So, we move forward and open up the space

00:36:23.410 --> 00:36:26.430
for discussions on antisemitism.

00:36:26.430 --> 00:36:29.450
That means not being so
quick to treat everyone

00:36:29.450 --> 00:36:32.530
as if they are David
Duke, or Louis Farrakhan.

00:36:32.530 --> 00:36:34.750
It means understanding

00:36:34.750 --> 00:36:37.890
that as we learn and
practice antisemitism,

00:36:37.890 --> 00:36:41.400
we are likely to stumble
and make mistakes.

00:36:41.400 --> 00:36:45.770
But if we unfairly penalize people

00:36:45.770 --> 00:36:48.260
because of their mistakes,

00:36:48.260 --> 00:36:50.850
we will shut down the very conversations

00:36:50.850 --> 00:36:53.380
we need to have in this moment.

00:36:53.380 --> 00:36:56.530
As I've said, as a
racial justice activist,

00:36:56.530 --> 00:36:59.690
one cannot fight racism in this country

00:36:59.690 --> 00:37:01.993
without being willing to experience it.

00:37:03.060 --> 00:37:05.540
None can fight antisemitism,

00:37:05.540 --> 00:37:07.970
another form of racism in this country,

00:37:07.970 --> 00:37:10.930
without being willing to experience it.

00:37:10.930 --> 00:37:13.240
It is the unfair burden

00:37:13.240 --> 00:37:16.173
of moving towards a
more equitable society.

00:37:17.430 --> 00:37:19.323
Lastly, I wanna say this.

00:37:20.270 --> 00:37:23.903
We have to understand the
moment we are in right now.

00:37:24.820 --> 00:37:26.520
We live in a country right now

00:37:26.520 --> 00:37:28.490
where synagogues are being attacked.

00:37:28.490 --> 00:37:30.350
They're not alone.

00:37:30.350 --> 00:37:33.870
We are in a society where
they are being set on fire,

00:37:33.870 --> 00:37:35.300
or Jews are being attacked

00:37:35.300 --> 00:37:37.890
on the streets of the United States.

00:37:37.890 --> 00:37:39.730
The Anti-Defamation League,

00:37:39.730 --> 00:37:42.530
the Department of
Homeland Security, the FBI

00:37:42.530 --> 00:37:47.110
had documented record
numbers of antisemitic crimes

00:37:47.110 --> 00:37:51.513
being reported over the last
two years, increasingly so.

00:37:52.418 --> 00:37:54.753
We have to recognize the moment we are in.

00:37:55.750 --> 00:37:57.800
We can not fight anti...

00:37:57.800 --> 00:38:00.430
We can not fight racism in this country

00:38:00.430 --> 00:38:02.640
without also tackling antisemitism

00:38:03.594 --> 00:38:07.757
and we can't tackle antisemitism
without tackling racism.

00:38:08.780 --> 00:38:10.440
If the injury and the assault

00:38:10.440 --> 00:38:12.810
on 140 law enforcement officers

00:38:13.810 --> 00:38:18.090
on the Capitol steps of Washington DC

00:38:18.090 --> 00:38:20.170
with little fanfare, or reaction

00:38:22.360 --> 00:38:25.010
does not tell you what
moment we're in right now,

00:38:25.010 --> 00:38:26.480
I fear nothing I'm going to say

00:38:26.480 --> 00:38:30.860
in the question and answer
period will convince you.

00:38:30.860 --> 00:38:33.840
But I will leave you with
this last final word,

00:38:33.840 --> 00:38:35.463
your role in this moment.

00:38:36.856 --> 00:38:39.550
When I was a kid, we grew up very poor

00:38:40.600 --> 00:38:43.610
and by summer most I and my other friends

00:38:43.610 --> 00:38:46.650
were out of resources and
you'll usually find us sitting

00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:49.713
outside of the apartment
building on the lawn.

00:38:50.720 --> 00:38:53.770
Every summer we would
remember this game we played,

00:38:53.770 --> 00:38:55.960
called, "If I were."

00:38:55.960 --> 00:38:58.507
And we'd sit in a circle and I went,

00:38:58.507 --> 00:39:01.027
"If I were driving down
the middle of the freeway

00:39:01.027 --> 00:39:04.420
"and the brakes went out,
here's how I would respond."

00:39:04.420 --> 00:39:07.250
And we'd argue about how we'd
respond, or how we wouldn't.

00:39:07.250 --> 00:39:09.483
What would do in that moment?

00:39:10.597 --> 00:39:12.970
"If I found myself in lion's cage,"

00:39:12.970 --> 00:39:15.497
dunno how that would happen,
"and the lion came out,

00:39:15.497 --> 00:39:17.047
"here's what I would do."

00:39:17.890 --> 00:39:21.053
But you know what question we
would always say every summer,

00:39:22.017 --> 00:39:25.967
"If I were in the midst of the
1960 civil rights movement,

00:39:25.967 --> 00:39:28.180
"here's what I would do."

00:39:28.180 --> 00:39:32.043
And boy, would we argue about
what we would, or wouldn't do.

00:39:32.947 --> 00:39:36.220
We didn't understand the
choices of our parents.

00:39:36.220 --> 00:39:39.300
We didn't understand
what it meant to grow up

00:39:39.300 --> 00:39:43.160
under Jim Crow, separate but equal,

00:39:43.160 --> 00:39:45.883
the hardcore racism of the 1950s.

00:39:46.820 --> 00:39:48.420
So, we were full of bravado

00:39:48.420 --> 00:39:50.523
about what we would, or wouldn't do.

00:39:51.510 --> 00:39:53.820
That question has always haunted me.

00:39:53.820 --> 00:39:54.960
What would I do

00:39:54.960 --> 00:39:58.150
in the midst of the 1960
civil rights movement?

00:39:58.150 --> 00:39:59.910
You may have played similar games

00:39:59.910 --> 00:40:02.280
with similar moments in history.

00:40:02.280 --> 00:40:03.603
What would you have done?

00:40:04.640 --> 00:40:07.990
Well, it occurred to
me about five years ago

00:40:09.020 --> 00:40:13.440
that I actually no longer
needed to ask that question

00:40:13.440 --> 00:40:14.973
and neither do any of you.

00:40:15.900 --> 00:40:20.900
The truth is this, whatever
it is we would have done

00:40:20.980 --> 00:40:22.943
in the midst of the 1960s,

00:40:24.340 --> 00:40:26.520
is the same thing we are going to do

00:40:26.520 --> 00:40:28.533
when we leave this talk today.

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:30.603
Make it count.

00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:35.363
Many people have sacrificed to
bring us to this very moment.

00:40:36.200 --> 00:40:40.310
The gateway to a multi-racial democracy.

00:40:40.310 --> 00:40:41.830
It won't come easy.

00:40:41.830 --> 00:40:43.760
There's no 30-minute sitcom

00:40:43.760 --> 00:40:46.390
where everything gets tied up nice.

00:40:46.390 --> 00:40:48.833
This calls for real work and commitment.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:53.840
To save democracy, you first
have to love democracy.

00:40:53.840 --> 00:40:57.730
To save the United States of
America, you first have to love

00:40:57.730 --> 00:41:01.330
the people in the United
States of America.

00:41:01.330 --> 00:41:04.140
That's what this moment calls for.

00:41:04.140 --> 00:41:09.140
Courage, leaning in at a
time of great complexity,

00:41:09.650 --> 00:41:13.510
understanding what is it that you will do

00:41:13.510 --> 00:41:15.903
for the 21st century
civil rights movement.

00:41:16.750 --> 00:41:18.460
Make it count.

00:41:18.460 --> 00:41:20.520
History will judge you

00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:23.083
and what you do in this moment, matters.

00:41:24.190 --> 00:41:25.300
Thank you.

00:41:25.300 --> 00:41:27.500
Now, let's take some
questions and comments.

00:41:28.510 --> 00:41:29.970
- Thank you so much, Eric.

00:41:29.970 --> 00:41:34.350
Really appreciate your
hard work here and always.

00:41:34.350 --> 00:41:36.220
We do have a number of
questions that have come in,

00:41:36.220 --> 00:41:41.143
so I'm gonna do my best to
send them your way verbally.

00:41:41.143 --> 00:41:43.980
I would just remind our
guests in the audience

00:41:43.980 --> 00:41:47.660
to please continue to
submit questions via the Q&amp;A

00:41:47.660 --> 00:41:49.113
if they have any for you.

00:41:50.260 --> 00:41:51.920
One question that's come in asked you

00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:55.160
to talk a little bit
more about dog whistling.

00:41:55.160 --> 00:41:59.430
And you noted terms like
globalist, or the media

00:41:59.430 --> 00:42:03.260
that have become important
stand-ins and dog whistles

00:42:03.260 --> 00:42:05.151
for antisemitism.

00:42:05.151 --> 00:42:06.710
And I think the question
asks, in particular,

00:42:06.710 --> 00:42:09.720
how you think this
persistence of dog whistling,

00:42:09.720 --> 00:42:12.250
or perhaps the new forms of dog whistling,

00:42:12.250 --> 00:42:14.640
might change how people
think in the university,

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:17.990
how we think about education,
how we think about the work

00:42:17.990 --> 00:42:22.380
that educators and students
are doing in 2021, 2022?

00:42:22.380 --> 00:42:23.580
Any thoughts?

00:42:23.580 --> 00:42:24.950
- That's a great question.

00:42:24.950 --> 00:42:27.640
Look, I think we see a number of,

00:42:27.640 --> 00:42:29.240
within the area of antisemitism,

00:42:30.390 --> 00:42:32.270
we see a number of dog whistles

00:42:32.270 --> 00:42:34.930
that are often put into play, right?

00:42:34.930 --> 00:42:38.240
The idea that somehow the Jewish community

00:42:38.240 --> 00:42:41.643
exerts more power and
control in a society,

00:42:42.740 --> 00:42:43.640
in society.

00:42:43.640 --> 00:42:47.490
We see that in rhetoric
across the political spectrum.

00:42:47.490 --> 00:42:51.420
I just think last week,
or the week before,

00:42:51.420 --> 00:42:54.010
former president,

00:42:54.010 --> 00:42:55.013
Mr. Trump,

00:42:56.330 --> 00:43:01.330
made a statement about how
Israel controls the United States

00:43:02.350 --> 00:43:04.460
and policies of the United States.

00:43:04.460 --> 00:43:08.680
Now, he said it as as a
philo-Semitic statement, right?

00:43:08.680 --> 00:43:11.920
Seemingly positive, like when people say

00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:15.390
Black people are so articulate,
or dance so well, right?

00:43:15.390 --> 00:43:19.120
These seem like positive
comments, but we understand

00:43:19.120 --> 00:43:23.360
that they are merely
reinforcing racist tropes.

00:43:23.360 --> 00:43:28.080
So, you see this often, this
idea of invisible Jewish power

00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:30.260
that is a significant trope.

00:43:30.260 --> 00:43:32.230
The other is blood libel.

00:43:32.230 --> 00:43:37.230
The idea that somehow Jews
are sacrificing children,

00:43:37.336 --> 00:43:41.220
or the vulnerable in a
society with no care.

00:43:41.220 --> 00:43:43.150
These are the two predominant tropes,

00:43:43.150 --> 00:43:45.980
but there are a number of historic tropes.

00:43:45.980 --> 00:43:49.100
I should say, for those
who study antisemitism

00:43:50.250 --> 00:43:52.630
and who are far better experts than I,

00:43:52.630 --> 00:43:56.290
I think it's important to
note that we all understand

00:43:56.290 --> 00:44:00.560
that these tropes predate
the origins of antisemitism.

00:44:00.560 --> 00:44:05.560
Antisemitism is a specific
form of anti-Jewish bigotry

00:44:06.100 --> 00:44:11.100
and it is an ideology, but
these tropes are very active

00:44:11.620 --> 00:44:13.820
in modern antisemitism

00:44:13.820 --> 00:44:15.990
and it's why we need to understand them.

00:44:15.990 --> 00:44:19.900
I think checking out out of the library,

00:44:19.900 --> 00:44:24.900
or getting a book by a good
academic who looks through

00:44:24.970 --> 00:44:28.100
the, "Protocols of the
Learned Elders of Zion,"

00:44:28.100 --> 00:44:29.760
is a good place to start.

00:44:29.760 --> 00:44:32.850
Most of the tropes are existent in there

00:44:32.850 --> 00:44:37.280
and if we understand the tropes,
we can then recognize them

00:44:37.280 --> 00:44:41.270
when they're in play and
we can point them out.

00:44:41.270 --> 00:44:42.350
We have a...

00:44:42.350 --> 00:44:44.970
For me, I understand by way of example

00:44:44.970 --> 00:44:46.860
and then we'll go to the next question,

00:44:46.860 --> 00:44:48.923
if someone starts talking about thugs,

00:44:51.330 --> 00:44:54.400
I have an idea to start paying
a little bit more attention

00:44:54.400 --> 00:44:57.620
to what they're saying
because I understand

00:44:57.620 --> 00:45:00.540
the thug is often of a dog whistle

00:45:02.120 --> 00:45:04.480
towards Blacks and Latinos.

00:45:04.480 --> 00:45:06.650
In the same way we have to become literate

00:45:06.650 --> 00:45:09.530
in the language of antisemitism.

00:45:09.530 --> 00:45:13.850
Until we do, all of us
will be manipulated by it

00:45:13.850 --> 00:45:16.300
no matter where we sit on
the political spectrum.

00:45:18.950 --> 00:45:20.520
- Thank you very much.

00:45:20.520 --> 00:45:23.570
The questions are coming
in fast and furious.

00:45:23.570 --> 00:45:25.900
We have a question here that asks

00:45:25.900 --> 00:45:30.347
about how white nationalists
and what this person calls,

00:45:30.347 --> 00:45:34.620
"White right-wing populists,
do invoke the discourse

00:45:34.620 --> 00:45:37.547
of civil rights when discussing
the supposed dispossession

00:45:37.547 --> 00:45:41.710
"of white people, or the supposed
silence of conservatives."

00:45:41.710 --> 00:45:43.080
Can you talk a little bit about this

00:45:43.080 --> 00:45:45.460
and whether you see it as a cynical play,

00:45:45.460 --> 00:45:46.803
or in some other way?

00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:53.400
- Well, we understand from
the inception, antisemitism,

00:45:53.620 --> 00:45:56.540
the narrative of
antisemitism, paints a picture

00:45:56.540 --> 00:46:01.430
that Jews are seeking to
destroy European Christendom

00:46:01.430 --> 00:46:04.450
In the United States race became

00:46:04.450 --> 00:46:08.790
much more of a primary
identifier than religion.

00:46:08.790 --> 00:46:11.090
So, instead of European,

00:46:11.090 --> 00:46:12.990
the structure of European Christendom,

00:46:13.974 --> 00:46:17.310
it became the destruction
of white Christendom

00:46:17.310 --> 00:46:18.143
here in the U.S.

00:46:18.143 --> 00:46:21.470
That is how antisemitism
is largely defined.

00:46:21.470 --> 00:46:23.310
We should understand that that continues

00:46:23.310 --> 00:46:24.940
to mainstream itself, right?

00:46:24.940 --> 00:46:29.640
It mainstreamed itself from
the term white genocide

00:46:29.640 --> 00:46:32.047
to the chants in streets
of Charlottesville,

00:46:32.047 --> 00:46:37.023
"Jews will not replace us,"
to Tucker Carlson promoting

00:46:38.000 --> 00:46:40.800
replacement theory,
which is just a retelling

00:46:41.700 --> 00:46:46.700
of the Protocols through
antisemitic tropes.

00:46:46.870 --> 00:46:48.440
At the end of the day,

00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:51.823
demographics are changing
in the United States.

00:46:52.800 --> 00:46:54.540
We are a diverse society

00:46:54.540 --> 00:46:58.320
going through a significant
demographic change.

00:46:58.320 --> 00:47:01.670
That creates demographic anxiety.

00:47:01.670 --> 00:47:06.110
Anxiety to demographic
change is actually natural.

00:47:06.110 --> 00:47:09.110
We who are on, and I put
myself on the progressive left.

00:47:09.110 --> 00:47:11.790
That's where I sit on
the political spectrum.

00:47:11.790 --> 00:47:14.550
This applies across
the political spectrum.

00:47:14.550 --> 00:47:18.730
We do a terrible job of
managing demographic anxiety.

00:47:18.730 --> 00:47:23.730
We actually tell people that
that anxiety is unnatural,

00:47:24.380 --> 00:47:25.730
or it's bigoted.

00:47:25.730 --> 00:47:30.010
But the truth is, all of us
experience demographic anxiety.

00:47:30.010 --> 00:47:32.650
We experience any time we walk into a room

00:47:32.650 --> 00:47:34.360
of people we don't know.

00:47:34.360 --> 00:47:38.520
All those feelings you're
feeling are demographic anxiety.

00:47:38.520 --> 00:47:42.450
We need to stop treating people
as if they are David Duke

00:47:42.450 --> 00:47:46.650
because they are feeling
the change of a society.

00:47:46.650 --> 00:47:48.380
On the other hand, though,

00:47:48.380 --> 00:47:52.230
white nationalists are exploiting
that demographic anxiety.

00:47:52.230 --> 00:47:54.770
They are telling those
who are experiencing it,

00:47:54.770 --> 00:47:56.600
that it's not natural, right?

00:47:56.600 --> 00:47:59.190
It's not natural to feel that anxiety.

00:47:59.190 --> 00:48:02.040
That it's an existential crisis

00:48:02.040 --> 00:48:04.980
and that they need to
prepare to defend themselves

00:48:04.980 --> 00:48:08.560
against that existential
crisis by arming themselves

00:48:08.560 --> 00:48:11.030
and preparing for a race war.

00:48:11.030 --> 00:48:14.920
We should understand that
in the midst of great change

00:48:14.920 --> 00:48:19.920
in a society under stress,
COVID, economic instability,

00:48:20.140 --> 00:48:23.410
political violence, climate change,

00:48:23.410 --> 00:48:26.140
that people will begin to believe that

00:48:27.147 --> 00:48:29.520
unless we put forward real policies

00:48:30.360 --> 00:48:33.690
that de-segregate this society.

00:48:33.690 --> 00:48:37.200
It is why segregation and racial profiling

00:48:37.200 --> 00:48:40.990
are the most significant
national security threats

00:48:40.990 --> 00:48:42.870
in this country today.

00:48:42.870 --> 00:48:45.790
What we understand about
demographic anxiety,

00:48:45.790 --> 00:48:47.920
is that it can be managed.

00:48:47.920 --> 00:48:52.480
It doesn't go away, but one
learns by putting themselves

00:48:52.480 --> 00:48:55.563
in unfamiliar environments
over and over again.

00:48:57.838 --> 00:48:59.638
When you have anxiety around flying,

00:49:01.030 --> 00:49:04.540
counselors don't tell you
to stop flying, right?

00:49:04.540 --> 00:49:06.810
What they tell you is
to start flying more,

00:49:06.810 --> 00:49:09.980
that there's a way to kind
of manage that anxiety.

00:49:09.980 --> 00:49:14.020
So, we have to get better
in terms of public policy,

00:49:14.020 --> 00:49:18.160
in understanding that the current
inequality in this society

00:49:18.160 --> 00:49:21.650
is killing American democracy.

00:49:21.650 --> 00:49:24.890
There is no bigger threat.

00:49:24.890 --> 00:49:26.250
And in terms of the management

00:49:26.250 --> 00:49:29.480
of the white nationalist
group, it is racial profiling

00:49:29.480 --> 00:49:32.410
that is the largest
national security threat.

00:49:32.410 --> 00:49:36.940
For months, law enforcement
in DC understood

00:49:36.940 --> 00:49:40.480
that white nationalists were
coming to that community

00:49:40.480 --> 00:49:42.560
in an attempt to disrupt

00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:45.380
the electoral process
of the United States.

00:49:45.380 --> 00:49:48.600
Yet on that day, we saw them,

00:49:48.600 --> 00:49:53.600
not in the population, you
know, crowd control, right?

00:49:53.670 --> 00:49:56.750
We saw them in very passive stance.

00:49:56.750 --> 00:49:57.830
Why?

00:49:57.830 --> 00:50:00.120
Because the folks who
were marching on that day

00:50:00.120 --> 00:50:03.060
weren't Black, or Latino.

00:50:03.060 --> 00:50:06.390
They didn't see them as
a threat and as a result

00:50:06.390 --> 00:50:11.390
they allowed 140 of their
fellow officers to be injured

00:50:11.750 --> 00:50:13.880
and five people were killed.

00:50:13.880 --> 00:50:18.503
It is that kind of racial
profiling, that unconscious bias,

00:50:18.503 --> 00:50:21.320
that is leaving the rest of us at risk.

00:50:21.320 --> 00:50:23.670
So, these are the issues
we have to contend with

00:50:23.670 --> 00:50:24.880
in this moment.

00:50:24.880 --> 00:50:26.670
Demographic change is real.

00:50:26.670 --> 00:50:28.620
That will continue to happen.

00:50:28.620 --> 00:50:31.280
How do we manage demographic anxiety

00:50:31.280 --> 00:50:34.160
and how do we get our policies to deal

00:50:35.335 --> 00:50:36.430
with the underlying segregation

00:50:36.430 --> 00:50:39.323
that exasperates that
anxiety in that society?

00:50:40.930 --> 00:50:42.090
- Thank you, we have several questions

00:50:42.090 --> 00:50:44.350
that I think are essentially asking about

00:50:44.350 --> 00:50:46.080
white nationalist leadership.

00:50:46.080 --> 00:50:49.060
And I think there may be a
way in which some people here

00:50:49.060 --> 00:50:51.110
may have heard you focusing on

00:50:51.110 --> 00:50:54.690
a sort of white nationalist
leadership that might have been

00:50:54.690 --> 00:50:58.680
somehow more community-based,
more working class.

00:50:58.680 --> 00:51:00.730
And so, several of these
questions are asking

00:51:00.730 --> 00:51:04.460
how you think about the
importance of wealthy donors,

00:51:04.460 --> 00:51:08.280
the Koch brothers as
mentioned in one question

00:51:08.280 --> 00:51:10.280
and other forms of
leadership, including people

00:51:10.280 --> 00:51:12.530
who are actually quite
enfranchised in society

00:51:12.530 --> 00:51:15.880
and might be pretending to
speak about those who are not,

00:51:15.880 --> 00:51:17.970
but about whom that could not be said

00:51:17.970 --> 00:51:19.760
applies to?
- Yeah.

00:51:19.760 --> 00:51:24.760
Yeah, I think often we project things onto

00:51:24.860 --> 00:51:27.680
right-leaning movements
that we would never except

00:51:27.680 --> 00:51:30.150
from our own movements on the left, right?

00:51:30.150 --> 00:51:34.830
We would never say that our
movements are controlled

00:51:34.830 --> 00:51:36.230
by rich philanthropists

00:51:36.230 --> 00:51:39.110
because we receive foundation grants.

00:51:39.110 --> 00:51:43.030
We would never suggest

00:51:43.030 --> 00:51:48.030
that we are being manipulated
by political elites above us.

00:51:48.480 --> 00:51:53.480
We treat our opposition
with a level of arrogance

00:51:53.530 --> 00:51:55.380
that is astounding to me

00:51:55.380 --> 00:51:57.630
and doesn't speak to the real issues.

00:51:57.630 --> 00:51:59.840
The truth is, is this,

00:51:59.840 --> 00:52:01.160
the white nationalist movement

00:52:01.160 --> 00:52:05.070
is putting out an effective
message and those who say

00:52:05.070 --> 00:52:06.650
that they're trying to
create alternatives,

00:52:06.650 --> 00:52:08.093
have failed to do so.

00:52:09.080 --> 00:52:10.920
Now, there are lots of challenges

00:52:10.920 --> 00:52:12.680
and there's lots of reasons

00:52:12.680 --> 00:52:15.100
on why the white nationalist movement

00:52:15.100 --> 00:52:16.800
has more wind than its sails.

00:52:16.800 --> 00:52:20.300
It's not just a failure of an alternative,

00:52:20.300 --> 00:52:24.670
but our ability to get
serious about this moment

00:52:24.670 --> 00:52:27.690
and understand that this
is not a question right now

00:52:27.690 --> 00:52:29.330
of economic inequality.

00:52:29.330 --> 00:52:32.830
It doesn't mean that economic
inequality isn't an issue.

00:52:32.830 --> 00:52:35.550
That this is an issue
of governance, right?

00:52:35.550 --> 00:52:40.200
Who gets to belong in
society is the key question

00:52:40.200 --> 00:52:43.030
that the other side is debating right now.

00:52:43.030 --> 00:52:44.850
And it is not just top-down.

00:52:44.850 --> 00:52:46.800
That is grassroots up.

00:52:46.800 --> 00:52:47.633
We see it.

00:52:47.633 --> 00:52:49.410
I often talk about this and this may be

00:52:49.410 --> 00:52:51.480
what people may be speaking to.

00:52:51.480 --> 00:52:52.580
I refer to

00:52:54.632 --> 00:52:58.363
a professor by the name of James
Aho at University of Idaho.

00:52:59.760 --> 00:53:04.460
In the early 2000s and I
think perhaps even till today,

00:53:04.460 --> 00:53:07.020
he's one of the few individuals

00:53:07.020 --> 00:53:09.420
who has done a substantial look

00:53:10.380 --> 00:53:12.180
at the white nationalist movement.

00:53:12.180 --> 00:53:13.400
He's a sociologist.

00:53:13.400 --> 00:53:16.847
He published his findings
in a book called,

00:53:16.847 --> 00:53:18.947
"The Politics of Righteousness,

00:53:18.947 --> 00:53:20.847
"Christian Patriotism in Idaho,"

00:53:21.794 --> 00:53:24.470
to look at the white
nationalist movement in Idaho.

00:53:24.470 --> 00:53:26.700
And he finds some interesting things.

00:53:26.700 --> 00:53:28.790
He finds, for instance,

00:53:28.790 --> 00:53:31.030
that the white nationalist
movement in Idaho

00:53:31.030 --> 00:53:32.790
has a higher level of income

00:53:32.790 --> 00:53:35.670
than the general population
of Idaho as a whole.

00:53:35.670 --> 00:53:38.170
That it is more highly educated

00:53:38.170 --> 00:53:40.723
than the general population
of Idaho as a whole.

00:53:41.560 --> 00:53:46.560
That is not unique when we look
at authoritarian movements.

00:53:46.630 --> 00:53:50.070
Outside the U.S. we see
that same trend, right?

00:53:50.070 --> 00:53:52.680
We should not think that because

00:53:54.090 --> 00:53:56.750
there are more working
class, or working poor people

00:53:56.750 --> 00:53:58.790
in these movements,

00:53:58.790 --> 00:54:01.330
that these are poor
working class movements.

00:54:01.330 --> 00:54:03.500
That just has to do with the demographics

00:54:03.500 --> 00:54:04.430
of the United States.

00:54:04.430 --> 00:54:06.667
There just happens to
be more working class

00:54:06.667 --> 00:54:09.720
and working poor people to draw from.

00:54:09.720 --> 00:54:12.720
The truth is, is that these
movements are disproportionately

00:54:14.792 --> 00:54:18.253
made up of upper middle class individuals,

00:54:19.565 --> 00:54:23.738
but they're not manipulating people

00:54:23.738 --> 00:54:25.970
who are working class and working poor.

00:54:25.970 --> 00:54:29.310
Instead, working poor and
working class folks are choosing

00:54:29.310 --> 00:54:31.020
one of the few alternatives

00:54:31.020 --> 00:54:32.900
that are being presented to them.

00:54:32.900 --> 00:54:36.950
Look, we haven't done a good
job on the racial justice side.

00:54:36.950 --> 00:54:39.700
We have not sent the message

00:54:39.700 --> 00:54:43.570
that white people are
also part of our formula,

00:54:43.570 --> 00:54:45.160
our way forward.

00:54:45.160 --> 00:54:48.463
And until we do a better job of that,

00:54:49.900 --> 00:54:53.390
people in the midst of
anxiety are going to cling

00:54:53.390 --> 00:54:57.400
to whatever they believe
makes them more stable.

00:54:57.400 --> 00:55:02.160
And in a racist society, a
society with unconscious bias,

00:55:02.160 --> 00:55:04.804
it is going to be the movement with bias

00:55:04.804 --> 00:55:07.920
(Eric chuckles)
that wins out in that race

00:55:07.920 --> 00:55:12.800
unless we come up with
better, more broader visions

00:55:12.800 --> 00:55:17.190
of what we mean when we
say America and Americans.

00:55:17.190 --> 00:55:20.193
So, I would just say
at the end of the day,

00:55:21.230 --> 00:55:23.380
yes, these movements are being funded

00:55:23.380 --> 00:55:26.393
through lots of diverse sets of sources,

00:55:27.240 --> 00:55:31.310
but I wouldn't be so caught
up on who's funding who.

00:55:31.310 --> 00:55:35.940
I would be more focused on
building real community,

00:55:35.940 --> 00:55:39.300
real mass-based movements on the ground

00:55:39.300 --> 00:55:41.780
that actually speak to people's needs

00:55:41.780 --> 00:55:44.440
and the conditions they're
living on right now.

00:55:44.440 --> 00:55:45.810
That's what's needed.

00:55:45.810 --> 00:55:47.710
We spend way too much time

00:55:47.710 --> 00:55:51.000
focused on the days of the
white nationalist movement,

00:55:51.000 --> 00:55:56.000
rather than the tools needed
to protect, defend democracy

00:55:56.650 --> 00:55:58.700
and manage this white nationalist threat.

00:55:59.930 --> 00:56:03.160
- Well, that's a good transition
then to several questions

00:56:03.160 --> 00:56:06.000
that have also appeared,
which really are asking you

00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:08.540
to think aloud, if you
would, about strategies

00:56:08.540 --> 00:56:11.320
for the left, or for progressive people.

00:56:11.320 --> 00:56:14.000
As people think about
building those coalitions,

00:56:14.000 --> 00:56:16.340
as people think about speaking back about

00:56:17.810 --> 00:56:19.070
raising fundamental questions

00:56:19.070 --> 00:56:21.310
about the embeddedness of antisemitism

00:56:21.310 --> 00:56:24.960
in national politics and
more folks are asking

00:56:24.960 --> 00:56:27.610
what gives you optimism
and where you think

00:56:27.610 --> 00:56:30.070
people's energies ought to go?

00:56:30.070 --> 00:56:31.270
There's a question, for example,

00:56:31.270 --> 00:56:32.800
about how we name these movements

00:56:32.800 --> 00:56:36.710
and how we name these
struggles for justice

00:56:36.710 --> 00:56:39.750
with antisemitism and
many other things in mind.

00:56:39.750 --> 00:56:41.840
And others are asking
questions, for example,

00:56:41.840 --> 00:56:44.550
about the place of labor unions and other,

00:56:44.550 --> 00:56:47.700
at least sometimes, progressive forces.

00:56:47.700 --> 00:56:48.940
So, could you talk a little bit about

00:56:48.940 --> 00:56:51.110
how you think about this strategically?

00:56:51.110 --> 00:56:51.950
Thank you.

00:56:51.950 --> 00:56:53.460
- Yeah.

00:56:53.460 --> 00:56:54.820
So, strategically

00:56:56.750 --> 00:56:58.560
I would argue

00:56:58.560 --> 00:56:59.393
that

00:57:01.210 --> 00:57:05.340
the most powerful wind we have in our sail

00:57:06.350 --> 00:57:08.303
is actually space and time.

00:57:09.800 --> 00:57:12.140
That almost sounds contradictory

00:57:12.140 --> 00:57:14.320
in the urgency of this moment.

00:57:14.320 --> 00:57:18.720
But what I mean by this
is, we have to understand

00:57:19.810 --> 00:57:22.880
something, I think,
really critically, right?

00:57:22.880 --> 00:57:25.150
That this is a backlash

00:57:26.790 --> 00:57:28.420
against

00:57:28.420 --> 00:57:29.890
winning.

00:57:29.890 --> 00:57:32.460
It is the racial justice movement

00:57:32.460 --> 00:57:35.210
that is winning in this country.

00:57:35.210 --> 00:57:40.210
Look, Black Lives Matters,
the movement in this country,

00:57:41.370 --> 00:57:46.200
in most polling that was
done previous to 2021...

00:57:46.200 --> 00:57:49.150
I haven't seen much pollings for 2021.

00:57:49.150 --> 00:57:54.150
But previous to 2021, Black Lives Matters

00:57:54.370 --> 00:57:59.370
was polling more support, by
percentage, of white America

00:57:59.620 --> 00:58:04.620
than ever supported Martin
Luther King Jr. in his lifetime.

00:58:06.280 --> 00:58:08.920
Black Lives Matters was
receiving more support

00:58:08.920 --> 00:58:09.840
from white America

00:58:10.824 --> 00:58:13.580
than the Student Nonviolent
Coordinating Committee,

00:58:13.580 --> 00:58:18.320
the sit-ins that took
place in the 1960s as well.

00:58:18.320 --> 00:58:20.940
Now look, we can look at those numbers

00:58:20.940 --> 00:58:24.593
and be sad that it's not
80% of white America,

00:58:25.740 --> 00:58:28.520
but quite frankly, we
should be more shocked

00:58:28.520 --> 00:58:33.520
that in a society that so
socializes people to other by race

00:58:33.860 --> 00:58:37.800
that such a significant
portion of white America

00:58:37.800 --> 00:58:41.270
would be pulling in support
of Black Lives Matters

00:58:41.270 --> 00:58:44.360
and that it's greater
than it was in the 1960s.

00:58:44.360 --> 00:58:48.460
That's an arc towards
equity and opportunity

00:58:48.460 --> 00:58:49.960
in this society.

00:58:49.960 --> 00:58:52.600
Again, look, I didn't grow up...

00:58:52.600 --> 00:58:55.010
I grew up in Southern California.

00:58:55.010 --> 00:58:56.470
I grew up very poor.

00:58:56.470 --> 00:59:00.170
I grew up through most
of junior high school

00:59:00.170 --> 00:59:01.960
and in high school

00:59:03.052 --> 00:59:07.000
in a motel that my mom paid
for the room by the week.

00:59:07.000 --> 00:59:11.100
So, I'm not a big fan
of the 30-minute sitcom

00:59:11.100 --> 00:59:15.290
where everything gets tied
up so nicely in the very end

00:59:15.290 --> 00:59:17.610
and all the answers get
questioned, you know,

00:59:17.610 --> 00:59:20.110
all the questions get answered

00:59:20.110 --> 00:59:21.980
and everything's so fair and happy.

00:59:21.980 --> 00:59:23.380
I don't know that world

00:59:24.219 --> 00:59:26.500
and I don't think very many
people in this country,

00:59:26.500 --> 00:59:29.270
or in this world, know that world.

00:59:29.270 --> 00:59:31.870
To know that world
where things get tied up

00:59:31.870 --> 00:59:35.440
so quickly and simply, is
just a world of privilege

00:59:35.440 --> 00:59:36.566
that is beyond my understanding.

00:59:36.566 --> 00:59:41.566
Where I live, where the most
people live in this country.

00:59:43.300 --> 00:59:48.300
look, struggle is a part
of advancing humanity.

00:59:48.490 --> 00:59:50.140
That's what it means.

00:59:50.140 --> 00:59:51.520
And you know what?

00:59:51.520 --> 00:59:53.650
It's terrible we have to do it

00:59:53.650 --> 00:59:57.960
and we shouldn't have to do
it so hard, but we really do.

00:59:57.960 --> 00:59:59.790
That's the job before us,

00:59:59.790 --> 01:00:04.020
to make it easier for the next generation,

01:00:04.020 --> 01:00:05.753
those who are yet to be born,

01:00:06.788 --> 01:00:10.040
to continue the path towards opportunity.

01:00:10.040 --> 01:00:12.093
This means, in my mind,

01:00:13.200 --> 01:00:15.420
letting go of this idea

01:00:15.420 --> 01:00:19.090
that simply because I demand a right,

01:00:19.090 --> 01:00:21.093
that it's simply gonna be given to me.

01:00:22.500 --> 01:00:25.410
I think it's just not
how history has unrolled

01:00:25.410 --> 01:00:28.430
and it's not how real life unrolls.

01:00:28.430 --> 01:00:30.520
So what, we have to get serious.

01:00:30.520 --> 01:00:33.210
We have to understand
that we have to continue

01:00:33.210 --> 01:00:36.790
to advance a vision verbally
of where we want to go.

01:00:36.790 --> 01:00:38.760
We have to get very pragmatic

01:00:38.760 --> 01:00:41.110
about those things that have been built.

01:00:41.110 --> 01:00:42.710
We have to stop rolling our eyes.

01:00:42.710 --> 01:00:44.180
I remember in the early parts

01:00:44.180 --> 01:00:46.873
of the Black Lives Matters movement,

01:00:47.760 --> 01:00:48.990
there was a great shirt.

01:00:48.990 --> 01:00:51.720
I actually loved the shirt
'cause I'm an old punk rocker

01:00:51.720 --> 01:00:53.783
and I like that kind of light sarcasm.

01:00:54.995 --> 01:00:56.697
It was a great shirt that said,

01:00:56.697 --> 01:00:59.270
"Not my Mama's Civil Rights Movement."

01:00:59.270 --> 01:01:00.493
Folks may remember that.

01:01:02.220 --> 01:01:05.330
I liked that shirt because it denoted

01:01:05.330 --> 01:01:10.020
this was a new generation
that had a new set of demands.

01:01:10.020 --> 01:01:11.860
And what was unique
about Black Lives Matters

01:01:11.860 --> 01:01:14.910
and what is unique about
Black Lives Matters,

01:01:14.910 --> 01:01:17.770
is that they understand the
things they are asking for

01:01:17.770 --> 01:01:22.380
aren't (sound cuts out)
as someone told me.

01:01:22.380 --> 01:01:23.680
These are basic rights

01:01:23.680 --> 01:01:26.460
that shouldn't even have
to be asked for, right?

01:01:26.460 --> 01:01:28.590
How should you even have to demand

01:01:28.590 --> 01:01:30.803
the idea that Black lives matter?

01:01:33.179 --> 01:01:36.090
How is that even a
controversial statement in 2021?

01:01:37.380 --> 01:01:41.770
And so, they were very
pragmatic in understanding

01:01:42.870 --> 01:01:46.693
that there was a very
specific conversation

01:01:46.693 --> 01:01:50.400
that they were attempting to
generate in the United States

01:01:50.400 --> 01:01:54.470
and I think they did so very successfully.

01:01:54.470 --> 01:01:58.930
We need more pragmatism
like that in the left,

01:01:58.930 --> 01:02:00.640
in the racial justice movement.

01:02:00.640 --> 01:02:02.460
Here's the second thing.

01:02:02.460 --> 01:02:07.460
We have to admit that we
really stumbled in this moment.

01:02:07.640 --> 01:02:11.060
For 30 years we ignored the rise

01:02:11.060 --> 01:02:14.410
of this white nationalist
movement and its impact.

01:02:14.410 --> 01:02:16.490
We rolled our eyes at it.

01:02:16.490 --> 01:02:17.740
We laughed at it.

01:02:17.740 --> 01:02:20.030
We laughed at those who warned about it.

01:02:20.030 --> 01:02:21.690
And we need to ask ourselves,

01:02:21.690 --> 01:02:24.250
how did we make such a stumble?

01:02:24.250 --> 01:02:28.720
If we can't ask and answer that
question amongst ourselves,

01:02:28.720 --> 01:02:31.550
how are we to understand

01:02:31.550 --> 01:02:35.030
and ensure that we don't
make those same mistakes

01:02:35.030 --> 01:02:36.100
moving forward?

01:02:36.100 --> 01:02:38.730
So, there needs to be much
more internal dialogue

01:02:38.730 --> 01:02:40.650
around who we are as movements

01:02:40.650 --> 01:02:44.050
and exactly where is it
that we are trying to go.

01:02:44.050 --> 01:02:47.030
And until we can answer that question,

01:02:47.030 --> 01:02:51.840
we can't expect the rest of
America to guess it for us.

01:02:51.840 --> 01:02:53.390
But there's a third piece here.

01:02:54.660 --> 01:02:55.720
I've often said

01:02:56.950 --> 01:02:59.950
that the goal of the
white nationalist movement

01:02:59.950 --> 01:03:04.280
isn't to target People of Color, or Jews.

01:03:04.280 --> 01:03:06.690
Yes, they do because it's affective.

01:03:06.690 --> 01:03:08.660
It's sending a message.

01:03:08.660 --> 01:03:11.800
It's effective at creating
the political theater

01:03:12.730 --> 01:03:14.510
that generates the conversation

01:03:14.510 --> 01:03:17.120
they want to have in this society.

01:03:17.120 --> 01:03:20.120
What I try to tell people all the time,

01:03:20.120 --> 01:03:23.875
is the real target is government, right?

01:03:23.875 --> 01:03:26.410
It's not People of Color
who are under attack.

01:03:26.410 --> 01:03:28.990
It is the government of the United States.

01:03:28.990 --> 01:03:33.610
It is the City of
Charlotte, the City of DC,

01:03:33.610 --> 01:03:35.700
the City of Portland, Oregon,

01:03:35.700 --> 01:03:38.600
the City of Los Angeles, California.

01:03:38.600 --> 01:03:42.090
It is actually government
that is under attack.

01:03:42.090 --> 01:03:45.790
And we have to begin to mobilize in a way

01:03:45.790 --> 01:03:50.100
that demands that government defend itself

01:03:50.100 --> 01:03:52.460
and defend American people.

01:03:52.460 --> 01:03:53.813
And we don't,

01:03:54.690 --> 01:03:57.440
we don't take that seriously.

01:03:57.440 --> 01:04:01.640
It means also entering government,
learning how to govern,

01:04:01.640 --> 01:04:06.160
understanding policy, the
boring day-to day-work

01:04:07.050 --> 01:04:08.810
of maintenancing

01:04:08.810 --> 01:04:10.880
a democracy.

01:04:10.880 --> 01:04:12.970
It's not as fun as marching.

01:04:12.970 --> 01:04:15.403
It's not as fun as making signs.

01:04:16.410 --> 01:04:19.030
But it is the work that
is needed to be done

01:04:19.030 --> 01:04:21.060
for the next generation.

01:04:21.060 --> 01:04:25.430
We have to stop thinking
that we are the gods

01:04:25.430 --> 01:04:28.930
that recreate society into our liking.

01:04:28.930 --> 01:04:30.350
That is a fantasy.

01:04:30.350 --> 01:04:32.830
That's not how the real world works.

01:04:32.830 --> 01:04:34.690
How the real world works,

01:04:34.690 --> 01:04:38.030
is that we invest our dreams
in the next generation

01:04:38.030 --> 01:04:41.860
and we urgently create space
for that next generation.

01:04:41.860 --> 01:04:44.780
And that means sustaining democracy.

01:04:44.780 --> 01:04:48.787
And that means taking governance
seriously in this moment.

01:04:49.920 --> 01:04:53.450
Elected board members, how
many school boards members

01:04:53.450 --> 01:04:55.523
are running unopposed this year?

01:04:56.746 --> 01:04:57.630
A record number.

01:04:57.630 --> 01:05:02.090
And then we're surprised
that these faux attacks

01:05:02.090 --> 01:05:04.010
on Black Lives Matters

01:05:04.010 --> 01:05:09.010
under the umbrella of critical
race theory are taking place,

01:05:09.620 --> 01:05:13.880
or that educators and
principals are being fired

01:05:13.880 --> 01:05:17.630
for talking about the
Holocaust, or slavery.

01:05:17.630 --> 01:05:20.600
It's because we are shirking our duties

01:05:21.866 --> 01:05:24.260
as changemakers in our society.

01:05:24.260 --> 01:05:25.510
We gotta get serious.

01:05:25.510 --> 01:05:27.610
If we don't take ourselves seriously,

01:05:27.610 --> 01:05:30.210
no one's gonna take us seriously.

01:05:30.210 --> 01:05:32.433
We gotta stop performing
and start leading.

01:05:35.220 --> 01:05:36.053
- Thank you, Eric.

01:05:36.053 --> 01:05:37.120
We're gonna need to let you go.

01:05:37.120 --> 01:05:39.346
I'm aware of that.

01:05:39.346 --> 01:05:40.179
Let me ask you at least

01:05:40.179 --> 01:05:41.012
one more question--
- Yeah.

01:05:41.012 --> 01:05:42.810
- if you've got a second.

01:05:42.810 --> 01:05:44.270
Somebody asked a follow-up question

01:05:44.270 --> 01:05:46.190
to the question that I addressed.

01:05:46.190 --> 01:05:48.370
I think it's trying to strike at

01:05:49.330 --> 01:05:53.310
the question of how advances in one area

01:05:54.510 --> 01:05:57.160
don't put to the side
important advances elsewhere.

01:05:57.160 --> 01:06:00.343
And so, the particular
question is about how,

01:06:01.340 --> 01:06:05.960
in activism surrounding BLM
over the last few years,

01:06:05.960 --> 01:06:09.570
many Jewish activists and
supporters may have felt

01:06:09.570 --> 01:06:11.930
that they became very
involved in these struggles

01:06:11.930 --> 01:06:14.570
and helped to push for justice equity

01:06:15.590 --> 01:06:19.160
and into police violence and
more in the very recent past.

01:06:19.160 --> 01:06:22.480
But at a moment, virtually simultaneously

01:06:22.480 --> 01:06:24.440
in which antisemitic violence

01:06:24.440 --> 01:06:26.030
and antisemitism more generally

01:06:26.030 --> 01:06:28.670
also appeared in the United States

01:06:28.670 --> 01:06:32.160
and elsewhere in the
world, may not have felt

01:06:32.160 --> 01:06:35.120
that Black activists,
Latinx activists and others

01:06:35.120 --> 01:06:39.790
stood similarly with them
to contest antisemitism

01:06:39.790 --> 01:06:42.053
in its violent and in its quotidian forms.

01:06:43.722 --> 01:06:47.420
How do we do that work
of assuring that again

01:06:48.620 --> 01:06:51.030
an important focus that comes on our radar

01:06:51.030 --> 01:06:55.330
for very urgent reasons,
doesn't in turn sideline,

01:06:55.330 --> 01:06:59.540
or eliminate from view
something like antisemitism

01:06:59.540 --> 01:07:01.713
as it emerges and persists?

01:07:02.740 --> 01:07:04.560
- Yeah, I would...

01:07:04.560 --> 01:07:06.870
Quickly, I wanna point folks to an essay.

01:07:06.870 --> 01:07:10.870
I throw my writings up
on, I think it's Medium

01:07:10.870 --> 01:07:14.990
because of kind of a DIY from,
lets say, an old punk rocker,

01:07:14.990 --> 01:07:16.520
so I just throw my writings there.

01:07:16.520 --> 01:07:20.690
I just have this thought,
who's gonna publish

01:07:21.680 --> 01:07:24.660
these writings, so I
just throw them up there.

01:07:24.660 --> 01:07:26.690
There's one I wanna direct folks to.

01:07:26.690 --> 01:07:28.690
If you Google my name and

01:07:30.261 --> 01:07:32.653
the essay, "Somebody Must be Blamed,

01:07:33.707 --> 01:07:36.550
"Antisemitism, the Equal
Opportunity Ideology,"

01:07:36.550 --> 01:07:39.570
so, "Someone Must be
Blamed," and Eric Ward,

01:07:39.570 --> 01:07:42.510
this fuller essay will pop up.

01:07:42.510 --> 01:07:44.380
But one of the things that I say

01:07:44.380 --> 01:07:45.940
that I think is critically important here

01:07:45.940 --> 01:07:49.230
is that antisemitism is emerging

01:07:49.230 --> 01:07:51.623
as an equal opportunity ideology.

01:07:52.947 --> 01:07:57.457
"Antisemitism crosses every
line of race, political party,

01:07:57.457 --> 01:08:00.483
"primary stance on a wide range of issues.

01:08:01.860 --> 01:08:02.727
At the time, I think I said,

01:08:02.727 --> 01:08:06.717
"Like the Corona virus,
this virulent ideology

01:08:06.717 --> 01:08:08.917
"disproportionately impacts
the Jewish community,

01:08:08.917 --> 01:08:10.980
"but in fact imperils us all."

01:08:10.980 --> 01:08:11.977
I went on to say that,

01:08:11.977 --> 01:08:14.747
"The Jewish community is
actually right to be concerned

01:08:14.747 --> 01:08:17.467
"in this moment of populous impulses

01:08:17.467 --> 01:08:21.167
"across the ideological
spectrum from the grievances

01:08:21.167 --> 01:08:24.917
"that propelled a B-list reality TV star

01:08:24.917 --> 01:08:27.877
"into the presidency to the cry of justice

01:08:27.877 --> 01:08:29.857
"that brings throngs of
people in the streets

01:08:29.857 --> 01:08:32.187
"in defense of Black lives.

01:08:32.187 --> 01:08:37.187
"Historically the populous
movements have always fed on

01:08:38.525 --> 01:08:42.940
"and in turn fueled
attacks on Jewish people."

01:08:42.940 --> 01:08:45.550
The Jewish community
has a historical right

01:08:45.550 --> 01:08:49.560
to be suspicious of
populism in the same way

01:08:49.560 --> 01:08:51.960
that the Black community
deserves the right

01:08:51.960 --> 01:08:55.000
to maintain its suspicion
of law enforcement

01:08:55.000 --> 01:08:56.330
in this country, right?

01:08:56.330 --> 01:09:01.270
These are historical documented
tensions and understanding.

01:09:01.270 --> 01:09:02.530
I don't think the Jewish community

01:09:02.530 --> 01:09:04.770
needs to say much more to us

01:09:04.770 --> 01:09:09.030
about why it is suspicious
and concerned about populism.

01:09:09.030 --> 01:09:14.030
Now, look, the onus is on
non-Jews to make this right

01:09:15.020 --> 01:09:17.510
and the way we make it right

01:09:17.510 --> 01:09:21.030
is by showing up on antisemitism.

01:09:21.030 --> 01:09:23.240
If there are law enforcement

01:09:23.240 --> 01:09:26.900
that I have to engage in
conversation, law enforcement,

01:09:26.900 --> 01:09:28.590
individuals, right, not the system,

01:09:28.590 --> 01:09:31.560
but individual law enforcement who I know

01:09:31.560 --> 01:09:33.770
have done some thinking on race

01:09:33.770 --> 01:09:35.913
and how it functions in a society,

01:09:36.940 --> 01:09:39.900
have a different set of
relationships with me

01:09:39.900 --> 01:09:42.620
than law enforcement who I know don't.

01:09:42.620 --> 01:09:46.040
And in the same way, if we
want the Jewish community

01:09:46.040 --> 01:09:49.670
to understand we're
serious about antisemitism,

01:09:49.670 --> 01:09:53.040
it means we have to start
tackling antisemitism.

01:09:53.040 --> 01:09:55.260
But I wanna say something
to the Jewish community,

01:09:55.260 --> 01:09:57.560
in particularly those
who are white-presenting

01:09:59.590 --> 01:10:01.200
it's simply this.

01:10:01.200 --> 01:10:02.870
You're exactly right.

01:10:02.870 --> 01:10:06.270
We can both be the victims

01:10:06.270 --> 01:10:10.993
and perpetrators of bigotry
at the same exact time.

01:10:12.010 --> 01:10:13.210
We have watched

01:10:14.090 --> 01:10:17.610
as a disproportionate
number of Black figures

01:10:17.610 --> 01:10:19.360
have come into the limelight,

01:10:19.360 --> 01:10:22.730
limelight around controversies
around antisemitism.

01:10:22.730 --> 01:10:25.090
If you understand the
nature of antisemitism

01:10:25.090 --> 01:10:27.870
and how it functions, it's
actually not surprising

01:10:29.040 --> 01:10:30.280
that a disproportionate number

01:10:30.280 --> 01:10:33.030
of Black and Latino individuals,

01:10:33.030 --> 01:10:35.770
vulnerable marginalized communities,

01:10:35.770 --> 01:10:39.420
tend to express the most
virulent forms of antisemitism.

01:10:39.420 --> 01:10:42.120
It's actually antisemitism
by design, right?

01:10:42.120 --> 01:10:46.110
The purpose of antisemitism,
one of the roles in Europe,

01:10:46.110 --> 01:10:48.120
was to create a buffer in society

01:10:48.120 --> 01:10:50.220
between the haves and the have-nots,

01:10:50.220 --> 01:10:54.690
so that when the have-nots got
frustrated, they were allowed

01:10:54.690 --> 01:10:58.190
to take their frustrations
out not on the haves,

01:10:58.190 --> 01:11:01.500
but this Jewish buffer
they were allowed to other

01:11:01.500 --> 01:11:04.310
and all the nefarious
things that were happening

01:11:04.310 --> 01:11:07.660
in the society onto that Jewish community.

01:11:07.660 --> 01:11:11.513
That was the Pilgrims
of the 1800s in earlier,

01:11:12.640 --> 01:11:13.750
in Europe.

01:11:13.750 --> 01:11:17.340
Well, that same theory of change

01:11:17.340 --> 01:11:19.550
still functions here in the U.S.

01:11:19.550 --> 01:11:21.360
and it's often why we see it.

01:11:21.360 --> 01:11:23.900
But I wanna say something else.

01:11:23.900 --> 01:11:25.670
We also have to acknowledge,

01:11:25.670 --> 01:11:28.520
that even as we condemn antisemitism,

01:11:28.520 --> 01:11:31.930
that unconscious racial
bias, anti-Blackness,

01:11:31.930 --> 01:11:34.700
plays out in these conversations, right?

01:11:34.700 --> 01:11:36.650
It doesn't make us bad to admit

01:11:36.650 --> 01:11:38.750
that these different dynamics

01:11:38.750 --> 01:11:40.930
are happening at the same time.

01:11:40.930 --> 01:11:44.820
I can tell you as a person
who wrote his first essay

01:11:45.830 --> 01:11:50.783
on antisemitism back in like 1992, '91,

01:11:51.730 --> 01:11:56.730
that Black folks who
stumble on antisemitism,

01:11:56.840 --> 01:12:00.270
receive a different level of response

01:12:01.290 --> 01:12:05.630
than non-Black folks who
make similar stumbles.

01:12:05.630 --> 01:12:07.630
I'm thinking right now of...

01:12:11.198 --> 01:12:14.030
I'm spacing on his name
right now, so apologies.

01:12:14.030 --> 01:12:17.253
The NFL player, DeSean Jackson,

01:12:18.560 --> 01:12:20.573
who made some really incredible,

01:12:21.610 --> 01:12:24.140
horrifying antisemitic statements

01:12:26.380 --> 01:12:27.660
on Twitter

01:12:27.660 --> 01:12:29.723
and to the press.

01:12:31.016 --> 01:12:32.330
You know, during that same week,

01:12:32.330 --> 01:12:36.770
Madonna said something
offensive and antisemitic,

01:12:36.770 --> 01:12:40.270
so did Chelsea Handler, I think it was,

01:12:40.270 --> 01:12:43.140
excuse me if I got that wrong,

01:12:43.140 --> 01:12:45.200
said something equally atrocious,

01:12:45.200 --> 01:12:49.030
but there was only one
person who received attention

01:12:49.030 --> 01:12:51.840
and that was DeSean Jackson.

01:12:51.840 --> 01:12:56.090
That is the unconscious
bias that exists in society.

01:12:56.090 --> 01:12:58.470
Now look, I'm not saying DeSean Jackson

01:12:58.470 --> 01:13:00.410
didn't deserve that attention.

01:13:00.410 --> 01:13:01.810
What I'm saying,

01:13:01.810 --> 01:13:04.510
is that if you're going
to give that attention

01:13:04.510 --> 01:13:07.100
to Black perpetrators of antisemitism,

01:13:07.100 --> 01:13:10.920
make sure you're giving the
same equal treatment and heat,

01:13:10.920 --> 01:13:12.460
to white perpetrators.

01:13:12.460 --> 01:13:16.000
If we don't do that,
we're creating wedges.

01:13:16.000 --> 01:13:17.750
But on the racial justice side,

01:13:17.750 --> 01:13:22.750
if we dabble in antisemitic
tropes, if we aren't disciplined

01:13:23.330 --> 01:13:27.970
in understanding that
antisemitism is a form of racism

01:13:27.970 --> 01:13:32.130
and if we are about racial
justice, if we're anti-racist,

01:13:32.130 --> 01:13:35.350
we have to oppose all
forms of racial justice,

01:13:35.350 --> 01:13:37.640
we are also creating wedges,

01:13:37.640 --> 01:13:40.770
wedges between two communities

01:13:40.770 --> 01:13:43.040
that have traditionally been the bedrock

01:13:43.040 --> 01:13:46.680
of civil rights in this
country since the 1950s.

01:13:46.680 --> 01:13:51.350
We each have to be more
responsible, stop pointing fingers

01:13:51.350 --> 01:13:54.350
and understanding that all of us function

01:13:54.350 --> 01:13:57.230
in an unconscious bias society.

01:13:57.230 --> 01:13:59.140
It doesn't make us bad people.

01:13:59.140 --> 01:14:02.230
What makes us bad people is being too lazy

01:14:03.168 --> 01:14:06.980
to learn what these are so
that we can try to avoid them

01:14:06.980 --> 01:14:09.080
because our children deserve that from us.

01:14:13.279 --> 01:14:14.579
- Thank you so much, Eric.

01:14:16.290 --> 01:14:17.700
I think we're gonna leave it there.

01:14:17.700 --> 01:14:19.860
I wanna thank you for
alerting us to what you call

01:14:19.860 --> 01:14:22.590
these stumbles over the last 30 years

01:14:22.590 --> 01:14:25.960
that, of course, you've been
working so hard to address

01:14:25.960 --> 01:14:30.780
across three decades now and
doing so much for all of us,

01:14:30.780 --> 01:14:34.280
for helping us to understand
better what's now at stake,

01:14:34.280 --> 01:14:36.860
the importance of thinking
about antisemitism

01:14:36.860 --> 01:14:39.540
within broader concerns about democracy

01:14:39.540 --> 01:14:42.920
in the United States and
worldwide and about anti-racism

01:14:42.920 --> 01:14:45.870
as a fundamental concern
of all of us and why,

01:14:45.870 --> 01:14:49.760
in your words, it's important
to show up in the right ways

01:14:49.760 --> 01:14:51.270
when it comes to antisemitism

01:14:51.270 --> 01:14:53.380
as a core concern for all of us.

01:14:53.380 --> 01:14:55.410
Let me just underscore
for everyone who's here

01:14:55.410 --> 01:14:58.590
that Eric's writings are posted
on Medium as he mentioned

01:14:58.590 --> 01:15:01.560
and I'd encourage folks to
read those articles carefully,

01:15:01.560 --> 01:15:04.810
where I think you'll find
even more to think about

01:15:04.810 --> 01:15:06.980
and answers some of the questions

01:15:06.980 --> 01:15:09.930
we weren't able to get to here verbally.

01:15:09.930 --> 01:15:12.340
Let me thank, in conclusion, my colleagues

01:15:12.340 --> 01:15:14.610
at Yale Center for the
Study of Race, Indigeneity

01:15:14.610 --> 01:15:17.670
and Transnational Migration and also

01:15:17.670 --> 01:15:19.900
the Yale Program for the
Study of Antisemitism,

01:15:19.900 --> 01:15:22.700
especially my colleague, Maurice Samuels.

01:15:22.700 --> 01:15:24.610
Eric, thank you so much
for your leadership,

01:15:24.610 --> 01:15:26.400
for your presence here today.

01:15:26.400 --> 01:15:29.000
And we'll look to you in the years to come

01:15:29.000 --> 01:15:31.040
to continue to be a
leader on these questions

01:15:31.040 --> 01:15:32.300
and so many others.

01:15:32.300 --> 01:15:33.610
Thank you.
- I look forward.

01:15:33.610 --> 01:15:34.683
Thank you so much.

